# No trailing slash ON PURPOSE: `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY only. Every tb-* worktree
# shares one install via a `node_modules` SYMLINK, which the slashed rule did not match — so
# `git add -A` swept the symlink itself into the tree (it shipped in c96ecec, pointing out of the
# repo into a sibling worktree). Slashless matches the directory and the symlink both.
node_modules
dist/
dev-dist/
*.local
.DS_Store

# --- raster art -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw masters NEVER enter git; only the webp the build produces from them does.
# The pipeline (scripts/optimize-art.mjs, wired into vite.config.ts) encodes anything dropped
# into public/images/<set>-jpeg/ and then MOVES the master into art-src/ — out of public/,
# because Vite copies public/ into dist/ verbatim whether git tracks it or not.
#
# NOTE: art-src/ is the author's LOCAL master library. git is not its backup.
# gitignore has no brace expansion, so each extension gets its own line.
# No trailing slash ON PURPOSE. A worktree shares one master library by SYMLINKING art-src at the
# other checkout, and `art-src/` matches a directory but NOT a symlink - so the link showed up as
# untracked and was one `git add -A` away from being committed as a link pointing outside the repo.
# (`node_modules` above is spelled without a slash for exactly this reason, and is why it never
# happened there.)
art-src
public/images/*-jpeg/

# Repo-wide, not per-directory. Path-scoped rules only cover the folders someone thought of:
# public/logo-i-light.png sat untracked and uncaught under the earlier per-folder version, and the
# next stray will land somewhere else again. Deny everything, then name the exceptions — that is the
# only shape of this rule that cannot be walked around.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# The exceptions, and the whole list of them. PWA manifest icons and apple-touch-icon are not
# reliably accepted as webp across platforms, so these five stay raster ON PURPOSE. Adding a sixth
# line here should require an argument.
!public/favicon.png
!public/pwa-192.png
!public/pwa-512.png
!public/pwa-maskable-512.png
!public/pwa-apple-180.png

# Author staging inboxes for raw art at the REPO ROOT. Masters live here until they are copied
# into public/images/<set>-jpeg/ for the pipeline; they must never enter git.
# The leading slash is load-bearing: unanchored `coaches/` would also swallow
# public/images/coaches/, i.e. the generated webp we DO ship.
/coaches/
/fields/

# Exported/generated save files. `tools/demo-save.ts` writes these, and serving one out of
# public/ is the only way to get a save into the running app (the file picker cannot be driven),
# so they turn up in the working tree routinely. They are throwaway state - two of them were
# swept into a commit on 29.07 and had to be filtered back out.
*.tsave
# ...EXCEPT the e2e fixture set, which is generated ON PURPOSE and committed. `tools/e2e-fixtures.ts`
# writes five career saves that Playwright seeds into IndexedDB before the app boots, so they are
# test data rather than throwaway state - regenerate with `npm run e2e:fixtures` (byte-identical
# every time) and see docs/plans/e2e-fixtures.md. The negation is anchored to the one directory:
# an exported save anywhere else is still ignored, which is what the rule above is for.
!e2e/fixtures/*.tsave

graphify-out/

# --- Playwright (e2e) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything a RUN produces, and nothing a run needs. `test-results/` holds the traces, videos and
# failure screenshots the config records on a first retry; `playwright-report/` is the HTML report
# (CI uploads it as an artefact instead - see .github/workflows/ci.yml); `blob-report/` is the
# per-shard intermediate a sharded run writes, which S3's nightly matrix will produce.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# The browser itself. Playwright downloads Chromium into a per-USER cache (~/Library/Caches or
# ~/.cache/ms-playwright), not into the repo - but PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=0 relocates it to
# node_modules, and CI recipes sometimes point it at a project-local folder to make it cacheable.
# Named here so that choice can never turn ~273 MiB of binary into a commit.
ms-playwright/
.cache/ms-playwright/
